            <div xml:id="d1227">

                <pb facs="0996" n="880" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg880"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2912.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Ciudad Juárez to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad Juárez</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">via
                                El Paso, Tex.</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1912-02-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>A communication received from Gen. Emilio Campa, commander of the insurrecto
                    forces, to notify all foreigners in Cuidad Juárez to seek a place of safety, as
                    his command will attack the city without delay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
